418746 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418762 1079 #uuid "96bf075f-8e0c-5f11-88cc-cf746d21f00c" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418763 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418751 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418763 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418752 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418763 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418753 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418763 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418754 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418763 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418759 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418763 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418763 1077 "selection" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418763 1078 #edb/ref 17592186418759 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418763 1079 #uuid "e0664c98-aa8f-5458-ad72-e93d50a1082f" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418764 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418737 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418764 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418740 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418764 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418742 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418764 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418743 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418764 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418758 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418764 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418764 1077 "selection" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418764 1078 #edb/ref 17592186418743 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418764 1079 #uuid "f71e16f6-f24e-58ff-9688-d083942b3ca5" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418765 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418738 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418765 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418739 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418765 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418741 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418765 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418756 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418765 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418757 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418765 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418765 1077 "selection" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418765 1078 #edb/ref 17592186418757 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418765 1079 #uuid "f7279778-d43a-559a-840e-ae02e897e9c9" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418766 1068 #edb/ref 17592186418765 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418766 1069 "q-140470" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418766 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418766 1071 "Find a basis of ${H}^{⊥}$ if $H=\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}.$" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418766 1072 #uuid "4a115f8b-a248-5ebc-93b2-6b42bb9d7f09" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418766 1074 "Let's denote the vector that spans the subspace $H$ as ${h}_{1}.$ \n\nA vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to ${H}^{⊥}$ if $x\\cdot {h}_{1}=0.$ So, we need to solve the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot {h}_{1}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M,$ which is already in row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, we have $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one), so ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are free variables. From the equation, we get ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{4}(2{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3}).$\n So, every vector in ${H}^{⊥}$ has the form \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}(2{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3}) \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of ${H}^{⊥}.$" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418767 1068 #edb/ref 17592186418764 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418767 1069 "q-80524" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418767 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418767 1071 "Given that $u=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]$ is a non-zero  vector that is orthogonal to the set $W={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]},$ find the value of $\\frac{b+c}{a}.$" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418767 1072 #uuid "95765da4-bd97-53db-8498-26a824409464" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418767 1074 "The vector $u$ is orthogonal to the set $W$ if $u\\cdot {w}_{1}=0$ and $u\\cdot {w}_{2}=0.$ So, we need to solve the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {w}_{1}=0 \\\\ u\\cdot {w}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ⇔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{1}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, we have $2$ pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd), so ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{3}=2,$ we get the vector \n$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, we obtain $a=1,$ $b=2,$ and $c=2.$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{b+c}{a}=\\frac{2+2}{1}=4.$" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418768 1068 #edb/ref 17592186418763 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418768 1069 "q-80514" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418768 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418768 1071 "For the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $u⊥H,\\,$ where $H={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$\n- $u⊥V,\\,$ where $V={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ \\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}]}$\n- $u⊥W,\\,$ where $W={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}$" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418768 1072 #uuid "ac83e377-f632-58f6-8bed-4004335968a6" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418768 1074 "Let's denote the vectors of $H,V$ and $W$ as ${{h}_{1},{h}_{2}},{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}$ and ${{w}_{1},{w}_{2},{w}_{3}}$, respectively.  \n\nNow, we have to compute the dot product between $u$ and the vectors in each set. \n\n- For the set $H:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {h}_{1} & =(-2)\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 0+(-4)\\cdot (-1)=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {h}_{2} & =(-2)\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot (-2)+(-4)\\cdot 1=-8\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u⊥̸H.$\n\n- For the set $V:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {v}_{1} & =(-2)\\cdot 3+3\\cdot 2+(-4)\\cdot 0=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {v}_{2} & =(-2)\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 3+(-4)\\cdot \\frac{5}{4}=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u⊥V.$\n\n- For the set $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {w}_{1} & =(-2)\\cdot 0+3\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot 3=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {w}_{2} & =(-2)\\cdot 4+3\\cdot 0+(-4)\\cdot (-2)=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {w}_{3} & =(-2)\\cdot 1+3\\cdot (-1)+(-4)\\cdot (-2)=3\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u⊥̸W.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418769 1068 #edb/ref 17592186418762 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418769 1069 "q-80525" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418769 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418769 1071 "Given that $u=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]$ is a non-zero  vector that is orthogonal to the set $W={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]},$ find the value of $\\frac{a}{b+c}.$" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418769 1072 #uuid "e54a7c62-bee3-5a5a-868c-0fd63367a8c9" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418769 1074 "The vector $u$ is orthogonal to the set $W$ if $u\\cdot {w}_{1}=0$ and $u\\cdot {w}_{2}=0.$ So, we need to solve the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {w}_{1}=0 \\\\ u\\cdot {w}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, we have $2$ pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd), so ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=\\frac{3}{4}{x}_{3}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}{x}_{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{3}=4,$ we get the vector \n$[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, we obtain $a=3,$ $b=2,$ and $c=4.$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{a}{b+c}=\\frac{3}{2+4}=\\frac{1}{2}.$" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418770 1058 #edb/ref 17592186418772 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418770 1062 #uuid "0577a2b9-4489-58d5-ac62-a197003874f0" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418770 1063 #edb/ref 17592186418769 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418771 1058 #edb/ref 17592186418770 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418771 1062 #uuid "35869f4e-ea24-507d-8562-2faa7b32b71c" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418771 1063 #edb/ref 17592186418767 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418772 1062 #uuid "76d46c90-8a7d-5c38-905d-f11edade0d5a" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418772 1063 #edb/ref 17592186418766 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418773 1058 #edb/ref 17592186418771 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418773 1062 #uuid "7791ae0e-534a-5b36-b058-c53eaf417327" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418773 1063 #edb/ref 17592186418768 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418774 1058 #edb/ref 17592186418773 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418774 1062 #uuid "c995944d-1a26-5669-9909-6a019a785d1b" 13194139534321 17592186045417 true] [17592186418774 1063 #edb/ref 17592186134228 13194139534321 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-127d383e-0561-515b-b9bf-949bec0e816d" 17592186418736 "answer-1a4730af-deb8-5685-8db4-054a0f26476b" 17592186418737 "answer-2560798b-15eb-58b9-9b21-90ea11e0e02c" 17592186418738 "answer-2fd54508-dbfe-5bf5-8588-0629d075c4dc" 17592186418739 "answer-45409e4f-d6f7-583a-a654-f6549650ec01" 17592186418740 "answer-4b9e698f-5a53-5e88-a9d0-bf26c7dc0622" 17592186418741 "answer-4bf16aae-72e1-5107-ae16-5b805fc64b24" 17592186418742 "answer-510cc82f-89b0-512e-a913-16359c5c9470" 17592186418743 "answer-5210b26c-a0e7-5a21-a878-831f0c686a70" 17592186418744 "answer-541db5fa-5828-53cc-9410-f2d882f278c7" 17592186418745 "answer-596addf6-8054-5598-9e84-8da605078378" 17592186418746 "answer-78313721-3417-534e-bd9d-